        "target": "First, let's identify the given quantities and the unknown:\n- Kevin spends 15 minutes to find each worm.\n- It takes Kevin 6 hours to find enough worms to feed all his toads.\n- Each toad eats 3 worms per day.\n\nFirst, convert 6 hours into minutes:\n6 hours * 60 minutes/hour = 360 minutes\n\nNext, determine how many worms Kevin can find in 360 minutes:\n360 minutes / 15 minutes per worm = 24 worms\n\nNow, since each toad eats 3 worms, we can find the number of toads by dividing the total number of worms by the number of worms each toad eats:\n24 worms / 3 worms per toad = 8 toads\n\nFINAL: 8",
